{"name":"Soft Blue Lavender","hex":"#888cba","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"soft","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily giving way under pressure.","Smooth and flexible; not rough, rugged, or harsh."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Be quiet; hold; stop; not so fast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soft"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/500px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/1280px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg/500px-A_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lavender serving as a nectar source for a small white butterfly","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_small_white_feeding_on_a_lavender_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo